# {{distribution}}

{{vendor}} provider shims for [llm-rosetta](https://github.com/Oaklight/llm-rosetta).

The provider tree is generated and checked by the core CLI; do not hand-write
its shape:

```bash
python -c "import sys; from pathlib import Path; from llm_rosetta.api import run_scaffold_check; sys.exit(run_scaffold_check(Path(sys.argv[1])))" src/{{package}}/providers
```

The contract it follows is documented in `llm_rosetta/shims/_shim_template/`.

## Install

```bash
pip install {{distribution}}
```

Installing registers the shims through the `llm_rosetta.shim_providers` entry
point. A gateway can also load the tree without installing the package, by
pointing `shims.paths` at `src/{{package}}/providers`.

## Layout

```
src/{{package}}/providers/{{vendor}}/
├── provider.yaml            vendor manifest: the shared credential and identity
└── <type>/[<format>/]
    └── provider.yaml        one leaf per lane
```

## Development

```bash
pip install -e ".[dev]"
pytest
```
